6. Tasks: Units of Work for Intelligence Agents 
A task is a procurement job assigned to one or more agents to execute autonomously. Think "Jira for procurement intelligence" — create it, assign it, watch the agent retrieve data, reason, and deliver results. 
Task Fields 
Title — what needs to be done 
Description — scope, data sources required, output format 
Priority — High / Medium / Low (auto-calculated from savings potential + deadline proximity) 
Assigned Agent(s) — which agent(s) work on it 
Status — Created → Retrieving Data → Analyzing → Brief Ready → Delivered / Resolved 
Output — agent's deliverable (negotiation brief, compliance report, talking points, submission status) 
Execution Log — step-by-step trace of data sources queried, reasoning steps, and tool calls 
