FAQs 
 
What are acceptable AI frameworks?  
All AI frameworks are acceptable, but you should not rely on a fully built, end-to-end application. What matters most is that you truly understand the framework you choose, embracing the principle: “You build it, you understand it, and you control it. 
What are the main core principles of this Hackathon?  
Every team participating in this hackathon will act as an ambassador, helping to spread the Agentic AI mindset within their own teams. 
What are the requirements for the infrastructure?  
All teams are free to use either Azure, AWS, or a hybrid of both, depending on what best fits their solution. There is no restriction on cloud providers, but cost-awareness and proper resource management are required. 
Every resource created during the hackathon must follow a standard tagging policy to ensure visibility, governance, and cost tracking. At minimum, the following tags are required: 
``` 
owner=team1 (or your respective team's name)   
product=hackathon  
costcenter=Mohalihub 
``` 
Should infrastructure be defined as code (IaC)? 
Yes. All infrastructure must be defined and managed using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) to ensure reproducibility, consistency, and easier collaboration across teams. 
Teams are encouraged to use tools such as Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, Azure Bicep, or ARM templates, depending on their preferred cloud platform. (Remember to install azure cli, aws cli or saml2aws to authenticate beforehand) 
Infrastructure should be version-controlled in a Git repository, and any changes must be applied through code rather than manual configuration in the cloud console. 
This ensures that: 
Environments can be easily recreated or scaled when needed  
Changes are auditable and traceable  
Teams can collaborate efficiently without configuration drift  
Solutions can be demonstrated and validated reliably by judges  